      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Libertarians often ground their critique in Lockean or Nozickian principles of self-ownership and justly acquired property. They argue that since an individual owns themselves, they own the fruits of their labor; thus, mandatory taxation is akin to forced labor or theft, violating fundamental moral rights. From the perspective of entitlements theory, any taking of justly earned resources without explicit consent constitutes a violation of that inherent right. This moves the argument beyond mere preference to a strict deontological claim about moral permissibility.",
